{"abstract":[{"text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inverted).","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Barlines have a location attribute to make it easier to process barlines independently of the other musical","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data in a score. It is often easier to set up measures separately from entering notes. The location attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must match where the barline element occurs within the rest of the musical data in the score. If location is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left, it should be the first element in the measure, aside from the print, bookmark, and link elements. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"location is right, it should be the last element, again with the possible exception of the print, bookmark,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and link elements. If no location is specified, the right barline is the default. The segno, coda, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"divisions attributes work the same way as in the sound element. They are used for playback when barline","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements contain segno or coda child elements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<barline>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","title":"MXLBarline","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/StyleColor"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/init(id:barStyle:footnote:level:wavyLine:segno:coda:fermata:ending:repeat:location:segnoAttribute:codaAttribute:divisions:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/barStyle","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/coda","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/codaAttribute","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/divisions","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/ending","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/fermata","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/footnote","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/id","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/Ivor